## Jōyō membership, ordering and gaps (15 October 2026)

- Raw KANJIDIC2 has 13108 characters. `misc.grade in [1,2,3,4,5,6,8]` yields exactly 2136 distinct characters. Grades count 80,160,200,202,193,191,1110 respectively, giving 1026 primary-school and 1110 secondary-school characters. Grades 9 and 10 are name-use categories and must not be included. (15 October 2026)
- All 2136 selected characters have their main SVG in `kanjivg-20260714-main.zip`. French meanings exist for 1987; 149 have none. Example gaps: 挨, 鬱, 𠮟, 剝, 頰. Rendering or pronunciation coverage does not prove French meaning coverage. (15 October 2026)
- [Bunka official 2010 jōyō table](https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/pdf/joyokanjihyo_20101130.pdf) defines the authoritative membership. [Current Bunka explanation](https://www.bunka.go.jp/seisaku/kokugo_nihongo/kokugo_shisaku/kyogikai/pdf/94217101_01.pdf) identifies 2136 characters. [MEXT current reading allocation](https://www.mext.go.jp/a_menu/shotou/new-cs/1385768.htm) links [the 2017 table used from school year 2020](https://www.mext.go.jp/a_menu/shotou/new-cs/__icsFiles/afieldfile/2017/05/15/1385768.pdf); its grade digits are the revised primary allocation. (15 October 2026)
- Explicit implementable order: grade 1,2,3,4,5,6, then grade 8. Within each group, ascending `misc.strokeCounts[0]`, then ascending Unicode code point `ord(literal)`. This yields a stable, useful progression now, with visible label “Par année scolaire, puis nombre de traits”. Grade grouping is official; the within-grade ordering is editorial. Keep `orderPolicy="grade-strokes-codepoint-v1"` in central settings. An official-table-order alternative requires extracting and verifying the source sequence first; raw KANJIDIC file order is not claimed to be official. (15 October 2026)
- Parent preference for official order can instead use the MEXT grade table order within grades and Bunka table order for grade 8, storing `officialTableIndex` per character. This inventory does not yet claim a verified machine-readable 2136-row official sequence. Do not infer rows from PDF text extraction without checking count, uniqueness, variants and all source pages. (15 October 2026)
- `misc.jlptLevel` is historical pre-2010 four-level data, as explained by [KANJIDIC producer documentation](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/KANJIDIC_Project.html). It must remain `legacyJlptLevel`, never directly modern N1,N2,N3,N4. KANJIDIC readings include readings outside the jōyō table, and nanori are name readings; do not label every dictionary reading an official jōyō reading. (15 October 2026)
- Preserve canonical characters and explicit variants. Bunka distinguishes canonical 頰/剝/𠮟 from forms such as 頬/剥/叱. A normalization rule must never collapse canonical IDs or remove supplementary-plane characters. (15 October 2026)

## Kana inventory contract (15 October 2026)

- SQLite contains no dedicated kana inventory. Reference dictionary entries containing kana are not a structured teaching table. Source facts can be verified against [MEXT kana chart](https://tsunagarujp.mext.go.jp/assets/download/hiragana_katakana_ver202210.pdf) and [Japan Foundation Marugoto Hiragana](https://a1.marugotoweb.jp/en/hiragana.php), with katakana counterpart linked there. Keep copyrighted charts/audio as links unless reuse terms explicitly authorize copies; build original layout from character facts. (15 October 2026)
- Per script, count 46 modern base characters including ん/ン and を/ヲ. Preserve gojūon order, leaving empty historical grid cells empty. Obsolete ゐゑ/ヰヱ are a separate historical extension. (15 October 2026)
- Per script, add 20 dakuten forms in g,z,d,b rows and five handakuten p forms. Include ぢづ/ヂヅ; homophony does not erase spelling distinctions. Do not inflate the base 46 count with these. (15 October 2026)
- Standard contracted forms are 33 combinations per script: small ゃゅょ/ャュョ after きしちにひみりぎじびぴ/キシチニヒミリギジビピ. These are combinations, not new basic kana characters. Rare ぢゃ etc. must be separately classified if included. (15 October 2026)
- Small っ/ッ is a distinct gemination item; small vowels, small ゃゅょ, long-vowel mark ー and iteration marks are separately classified. Particle readings は=wa, へ=e, を=o require usage notes, not replacement of letter readings. (15 October 2026)
- Modern foreign-sound katakana combinations such as ファ,ティ,ヴァ,ウィ belong to an extended table sourced from [Bunka 外来語の表記](https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/gairai/index.html), whose first and second tables have distinct scope. Do not generate every consonant-vowel cross-product as a valid Japanese sound. (15 October 2026)

